WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Dead bacteria changed living bacteria into the dead donor's type.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.960
What crossed between them?

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:12.100
Living rough cells usually lacked a capsule and were generally harmless.

4
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.340
Heat-killed smooth cells could not grow.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Yet mixing them sometimes produced living, capsule-bearing cells of the donor type.

6
00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.320
Their descendants kept that type.

7
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.100
Neither ingredient alone produced that outcome.

8
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:36.487
Griffith's mouse experiment revealed transformation, a heritable change in bacterial

9
00:00:36.487 --> 00:00:40.247
type. It did not name the substance responsible.

10
00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.847
But it pointed to an assay.

11
00:00:44.227 --> 00:00:46.487
Later laboratories moved it into culture.

12
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:52.587
Add a donor extract to rough recipients, then count colonies with the donor capsule.

13
00:00:53.847 --> 00:00:57.327
The active material could now be followed through purification.

14
00:00:57.327 --> 00:01:00.647
A scored phenotype replaced guesswork.

15
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:06.490
Researchers purified the active fraction, then challenged separate samples with

16
00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:11.750
enzymes. Protein-digesting enzymes left transformation active.

17
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.950
An RNA-digesting enzyme also left it active.

18
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.970
Each enzyme was first checked against a known target.

19
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.930
Now predict the decisive test.

20
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:29.630
If intact DNA is required, what should happen after a DNA-depolymerizing treatment?

21
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:39.647
The DNA-depolymerizing preparations removed activity.

22
00:01:41.387 --> 00:01:46.167
Chemistry also matched nucleic acid, and transformed cells passed the donor type

23
00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.207
through generations.

24
00:01:48.947 --> 00:01:53.187
Avery, MacLeod and McCarty concluded that the fraction was principally, if not

25
00:01:53.187 --> 00:01:58.607
solely, DNA. Their methods could not exclude a protein below detection.

26
00:01:58.607 --> 00:02:02.687
The hedge preserved the experiment's detection limit.

27
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.800
One system was not enough.

28
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:12.360
Hershey and Chase turned to phage T2, a virus of E. coli built from a protein coat

29
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.760
around DNA. They marked sulfur-containing protein with one tracer and

30
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.600
phosphorus-rich DNA mostly with another.

31
00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.640
The film keeps protein gold and DNA blue.

32
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.340
Where each color travelled could separate their roles.

33
00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.960
This was an independent physical test.

34
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:35.423
Both phage batches attached to bacteria.

35
00:02:36.903 --> 00:02:41.983
Blending removed material still outside, and centrifugation separated cells from

36
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:45.903
fluid. Most gold sulfur moved into the fluid.

37
00:02:47.203 --> 00:02:48.723
Much less blue phosphorus did.

38
00:02:49.883 --> 00:02:54.383
The stripped cells still produced phage, and progeny carried far more parental

39
00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:55.763
phosphorus than sulfur.

40
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.843
Exact percentages are on screen.

41
00:02:59.967 --> 00:03:01.527
The tracers set limits.

42
00:03:02.967 --> 00:03:07.847
Sulfur could not report sulfur-free material, so the experiment did not show that no

43
00:03:07.847 --> 00:03:11.787
protein entered. Some sulfur stayed cell-associated.

44
00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:14.347
That distinction matters.

45
00:03:15.547 --> 00:03:19.727
The result was narrower: most DNA entered, and most coat stayed out.

46
00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.687
Inheritance travelled mainly with the DNA label.

47
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.960
Across two independent systems, heritable change followed DNA.

48
00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.440
Transformation required intact DNA in a purified fraction.

49
00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.280
Phage reproduction followed the DNA-rich tracer into cells and progeny.

50
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.880
Neither experiment claimed more than it measured.

51
00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.680
Convergence, not one perfect experiment, carried the argument.

52
00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:54.840
Together, they made DNA the strongest candidate for inherited information in these

53
00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:55.240
systems.
